\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Geometry-controlled multi-view texturing and the TCAS intervention. The reference (camera 014), representative normal/depth/mask maps and six C3 outputs share one Fresh C UID; output cameras retain their recorded order. TCAS supplies the requested temporal profile. The existing native wrapper cap determines the applied scale, which multiplies the GeoTex residual before frozen-feature addition. Deep/middle retain 1.25/2.50/1.25; shallow remains 0.80. Equal applied scales do not imply equal corrections. The isolated bake panel shows a real native UV atlas and unseen camera 004 from a different Bake10 UID, with only transparent render margins removed. Appearance differences are preserved; this example does not demonstrate high-fidelity copying. Source identities and credits are in Supplementary Section\nobreakspace  {}S9.}}{4}\protected@file@percent }
